From dac01089cf8138aaac47280276f287aeebc3418f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 07:26:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redefine target with volatility-scaled band, add OOF stacking
 ensemble and Samsung-specific features

- TARGET_MODE (close_to_close | open_to_close) and BAND_MODE (fixed | vol_scaled,
  default 0.3 x 20-day vol, computed from d-1 data only) in the config cell
- New features: SK Hynix, London Samsung GDR (SMSN.IL) and GDR-minus-Samsung
  overnight signal, calendar dummies; open_to_close mode adds the 09:00 gap
- New section 6.5: OOF stacking (multinomial logistic on log-probabilities),
  trained on previous folds only, plus a mean-ensemble comparison and a
  per-fold balanced-accuracy table
- Live performance-weighted ensemble now uses full walk-forward OOF log loss
  (min 250 days) instead of the ~60-day Kronos common window; adds Stacked
  live forecast
- Kronos uses the per-date band and the open price in open_to_close mode
- Multi-horizon regression reports a zero-return baseline MAE and warns when
  a model is worse than it
- Fix failing test (price_close vs sam_close), compile every code cell, and
  test the new leakage rules
